\caption(Three unequal byte positions contribute exactly three units; the table preserves the original positions and cumulative count.)
\alttext(The two seven-letter words appear in aligned columns with red markers at positions two, three and four. A table lists unsigned byte values, mismatch indicators and their cumulative sum.)


>> A changed byte is not necessarily a single changed bit

Compare one raw byte 0x00 with one raw byte 0xff. The byte distance is one; their
packed-bit distance is eight. Writing those bytes as `00000000` and `11111111`
changes the representation to eight ASCII positions, so that string distance is eight.
The NUL is a real byte in the explicitly length-constructed string, not an empty string.
For unequal lengths, the example captures the documented exception instead of padding.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hamming_bits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  const std::string zero(1,'\0'),ones(1,static_cast<char>(255));dm::dstruct::DataFrame results;
  results.add_column("representation",std::vector<std::string>{"one raw byte","eight ASCII bit positions","packed unsigned word"});results.add_column("distance",std::vector<double>{double(dm::algorithms::hamming_distance(zero,ones)),double(dm::algorithms::hamming_distance("00000000","11111111")),double(dm::algorithms::hamming_bit_distance(0,255))});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::algorithms::plot_hamming_comparison("00000000","11111111").title("Eight bits changed inside one byte").size(900,340).save_svg("build/hamming_bits.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\nRaw byte values:\n\n{}\n",results.to_md(0),dm::algorithms::hamming_comparison(zero,ones).to_md(0));
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::hamming_distance("abc","ab");}catch(const std::invalid_argument& e){std::print("\nUnequal lengths: {}\n",e.what());}
}
```
